> Im using gemma 4 with custom provider and modalities option didn't work. But I was missing typing `"npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatiple"` in provider, and it worked after configuring it.

It seems like the image understanding of capable models is still not used for all providers in OpenCode. I've tested this with various Ollama models capable of image usage. Other software tools (e.g. Open WebUI) or a simple Python script are also able to use the models capabilities. I do not understand why it is not available by default in OpenCode though...

The setup that worked for me was to use `"modalities": { "input": ["image", "text"], "output": ["text"] }` in the opencode.json alongside with the `"npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"`.

Here is my config json example where ONLY `gemma4:12b-it-q4_K_M` works as it has the **modalities** addition:

```json
{
	"$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
	"provider": {
		"ollama": {
			"models": {
				"qwen3.6:27b-q4_K_M": {
					"_launch": true,
					"name": "qwen3.6:27b-q4_K_M"
				},
				"gemma4:26b-a4b-it-q4_K_M": {
					"name": "gemma4:26b-a4b-it-q4_K_M"
				},
				"gemma4:12b-it-q4_K_M": {
					"name": "gemma4:12b-it-q4_K_M",
                                        "modalities": { "input": ["image", "text"], "output": ["text"] }
				},
				"gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M": {
					"name": "gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M"
				},
				"qwen3-vl:8b-instruct-q4_K_M": {
					"name": "qwen3-vl:8b-instruct-q4_K_M"
				},
				"ministral-3:14b-instruct-2512-q4_K_M": {
					"name": "ministral-3:14b-instruct-2512-q4_K_M"
				}

			},
			"name": "Ollama",
			"npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
			"options": {
				"baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"
			}
		}
	}
}
```

If you would want to use images with the other models, you would need to add ` "modalities": { "input": ["image", "text"], "output": ["text"] }` , too.

For anyone using an Ollama instance, here's a simple Python script for you to test if the model supports image input:
However, you could also have a look at the model description on `https://ollama.com/library/<YOUR-MODEL>/tags`

```python
from tkinter import Tk, filedialog

import ollama
from rich.console import Console
from rich.markdown import Markdown

def image_vision():

    root = Tk()
    root.withdraw()

    image_path = filedialog.askopenfilename(defaultextension=".jpg", filetypes=[("Image files", "*.jpg"), ("Image files", "*.png"), ("Image files", "*.jpeg")])

    response = ollama.chat(
        model='YOUR-MODEL-NAME', # e.g. gemma4:12b-it-q4_K_M
        messages=[{
            'role': 'user',
            'content': 'What is in this image? If it is text extract the text and write it as Markdown. If there is no text describe the image. Answer in Spanish.',
            'images': [image_path]
        }]
    )

    console = Console()
    console.print(response)
    console.print(Markdown("## Response"))
    console.pri

